  <div class="col" style="margin-top:14px">
    <h3>Try this</h3>
    <ul class="tight">
      <li><em>Roof load only</em> is a frame 12 m wide with legs 4 m tall and a crown 3 m above the corners. The roof carries 6 kN for every metre, 72 kN in all, so each foot carries 36 kN. Each foot is also pushed inward with 15.43 kN, which is 6 × 12² / (8 × 7) with the crown 7 m above the feet. The moment is −61.71 kN·m at both corners, with the outside stretched, and exactly zero at the crown.</li>
      <li><em>Higher crown</em> raises the crown to 6 m above the corners. The upward forces stay at 36 kN, because they depend on the load alone, but the push at each foot falls from 15.43 to 10.8 kN, and the moment at the corners from −61.71 to −43.2 kN·m. The higher crown gives the push a longer lever arm.</li>
      <li><em>Level roof</em> takes the rise away, so the crown is only as high as the corners and the frame is closer to a beam with a pin in the middle. The push grows to 27 kN and the moment at the corners to −108 kN·m, and that is the largest moment in the frame.</li>
      <li><em>Wider frame</em> makes the frame 20 m wide. The roof load is then 120 kN and each foot carries 60 kN. The push is 42.86 kN, nearly three times the push of the first frame, because it grows with the square of the width.</li>
      <li><em>Load from the side</em> adds 2 kN/m on the left leg, 8 kN in all. The left foot is relieved, with 34.67 kN, and the right foot carries 37.33 kN. The feet are pushed inward with 8.571 kN and 16.57 kN, so the right foot is pushed harder, and together the two sideways forces are −8 kN, which holds the sideways load. The moment at the left corner is −50.29 kN·m and at the right corner −66.29 kN·m.</li>
      <li>Press <em>Roof load only</em> and then <em>Crown</em> next to Cut at. The bending moment is zero there, but the normal force is −13.8 kN, so the pin passes a force on but no moment. Press <em>Left corner</em> and look at the three tiles for the cut. The leg carries −36 kN in compression and the shear force of the leg is −15.43 kN, which is the push of the floor on the foot.</li>
      <li>Press <em>Reset all</em> and then drag the load on the roof from 6 to 12 kN/m. The line under the tiles reads upward at B +100 %, sideways at the feet +100 % and largest moment +100 %. Everything in the frame is proportional to the load, so every force and every moment doubles.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
